Chapter: RvTrapReport
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 `__narrow` admits 300 into a field bounded 0..150, so the range check
 traps: `ebreak` on riscv, `brk #1` on arm64. After `before`, riscv must end on
 `!EXC=0000000000000003 PC=<inside mk> TVAL=0` and arm64 on
 `!A64FAULT ... ESR=00000000F2000001 ELR=<inside mk>`. Before main 26347 the
 riscv run went silent after `before`; before the arm64 fix beside it, arm64
 printed `v 300` and `after`. Run it by copying it into `codex/test` with an
 `.expected` of `before`, then
 `build/test-cross-batch.ps1 -Arch <riscv64|arm64> -Filter <name> -Jobs 1`,
 which files it FAIL_RUNTIME with the fault line as the reason. It cannot
 live in `codex/test`: x86 traps on the same `__narrow`.

Section: Entry

  Box = record {
    v : Integer between 0 and 150
  }

  mk : Integer -> Box
  mk (n) = Box { v = __narrow n }

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni "before"
    print-line-uni ("v " & show ((mk (text-length "abc" * 100)).v))
    print-line-uni "after"
  end
